Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/pmc/buffer_read_adaptor.h>
#include <hexi/pmc/buffer_write_adaptor.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

struct TypedData {
    uint32_t id;
    int16_t value;
    double ratio;
};

std::vector<uint8_t> write_typed_data(const TypedData& data) {
    // Create a buffer and write adaptor
    std::vector<uint8_t> buffer;
    hexi::pmc::buffer_write_adaptor<std::vector<uint8_t>> writer(buffer, hexi::pmc::init_empty);

    // Write each field using the template write method
    writer.write(data.id);
    writer.write(data.value);
    writer.write(data.ratio);

    return buffer;
}

TypedData read_typed_data(const std::vector<uint8_t>& buffer) {
    // Create a mutable copy of the buffer for the read adaptor
    std::vector<uint8_t> buffer_copy = buffer;
    hexi::pmc::buffer_read_adaptor<std::vector<uint8_t>> reader(buffer_copy, hexi::pmc::init_empty);

    // Read each field using the template read method
    TypedData data;
    reader.read(&data.id);
    reader.read(&data.value);
    reader.read(&data.ratio);

    return data;
}
```

**Key implementation details:**

1. **`write_typed_data`**:
   - Creates an empty `std::vector<uint8_t>` buffer
   - Constructs a `buffer_write_adaptor` with `init_empty` to start from offset 0
   - Uses `write(auto& source)` template method for each field, which automatically writes `sizeof(field)` bytes
   - Returns the populated buffer

2. **`read_typed_data`**:
   - Creates a mutable copy of the input buffer (required by `buffer_read_adaptor`)
   - Constructs a `buffer_read_adaptor` with `init_empty`
   - Uses `read(T* destination)` template method for each field, which automatically reads `sizeof(T)` bytes
   - Returns the reconstructed `TypedData` struct

The template methods handle type-safe serialization automatically based on the size of each type (uint32_t = 4 bytes, int16_t = 2 bytes, double = 8 bytes).

